you know him as a jackass a wild boy and  a party boy but how much do you really  know about chris pontius this is the  untold truth of the jackass forever star  big brother is to jackass what the  national lampoon magazine is to its  better known film classics like  caddyshack animal house and vacation the  subversive skate magazine was run by  people like eventual jackass ringmaster  jeff tremaine and videographer spike  jones and it brought together the west  coast half of the original core jackass  crew johnny knoxville shot himself with  a gun for a big brother article jason  weyman acuna worked there and chris  pontius was first interviewed by the  magazine in 1992 as a young skater who  quickly became so much more than just a  one-time featured figure pontius would  go on to write for the magazine for a  while his talents obviously extended  beyond his skating career since he even  starred in some of the publications  movies which were full-on proto-jackass  extravaganzas he eventually ended up  getting fired by big brother but you  know how the story worked out from there  when the magazine's video team started  looking at making a show for mtv his  former colleagues decided that he had a  little special something they were  looking for that thing being a  willingness to parade around the world  in a thong for the sake of comedy  as chris pontius told the hollywood  reporter he was nude and in big brother  before he was even 18. although this  would technically be against the law  somehow no legal hammers came down from  day one though pontius felt comfortable  being in as little clothes as possible  in front of the camera pontius's first  big character was named party boy a  rambunctious herald of good times who  would enter a place tear off his clothes  and dance around in skimpy underwear the  show was on mtv so he couldn't go own  natural but he got about as close as he  could to the audience's delight there  was even a jackass kit in which the  self-starter stuntman posed for a nude  photo shoot with the ambition of getting  into the pages of playgirl on a show  where everybody hurts themself in a very  real way it's a testament to pontius's  natural charisma that he was able to  keep people entertained and make a name  for himself simply by taking off his  clothes  you might think the idea of porch  pirating stealing packages off of  somebody else's porch is a jackass thing  but you'd be wrong the crew hurt  themselves but never anybody else and  would never consider it funny to steal  from the average homeowner and given how  hardcore these guys are they'd  definitely be the wrong ones to target  especially the savage chris pontius he  recently landed in the news when footage  from his front door caught a guy  stealing a package off his porch that  was meant for his wife as the guy walked  off with the box pontius ran out the  door and took off after him he then  posted the footage to his instagram and  made a big report he was prescient  enough to catch footage of the guy's car  and info on his way out which is pretty  impressive it sounds like pontius didn't  manage to find the guy though because if  he had there probably would have been a  fight  it's tough to imagine chris pontius the  constantly smiling and laughing member  of the jackass family being a fighter  but apparently he knows how to scrap in  an october 2020 interview on stevo's  podcast pontius detailed a few of his  fights he explains how occasionally his  friends would start a fight only to  leave him holding the bag and having to  take on eight guys at once growing up  fist fighting seemed like a really  important thing to  to be able to do in a famous jackass  skit where he dresses as the devil and  campaigns to keep god out of california  a passerby punches him and pontius is  completely unfazed apparently there was  even a situation where pontius and stevo  passed out eggs to an audience and told  them to launch them at the band electric  6. the band didn't appreciate it and  allegedly threw a beer at stevo and his  date pontius then put on a wrestling  singlet and ran to their trailer  challenging them to a fight when the  band continued hiding in their trailer  he punched in a window until security  came  there's a pretty legendary episode of  mtv's cribs in which chris pontius tours  the audience around his house at toyota  tacoma it has to be at the top of the  list of all-time hilarious crib segments  as pontius walks the camera through the  vehicle eventually exploring the bed  where he goes through all his g-strings  and costumes van halen headband 1984. in  his interview on stevo's podcast pontius  discusses the fact that he was traveling  so much back then and always had so many  couches he could sleep on that he was  homeless by choice stevo reveals that he  was too but he gave up the life before  pontius did so how long did chris  essentially live out of a toyota tacoma  according to party boy himself he was  homeless for eight years we saved a lot  i mean i i know i yeah we saved a lot of  money on rent and and just i mean  there was no reason to have a residence  wild boys is a nature show unlike any  other combining the appreciation of wild  animals with the type of insane stunts  that made pontius stevo and the jackass  crew famous from swimming with great  whites to playing with snakes it is  equal parts educational and extreme the  show is also the realization of one of  chris pontius's boyhood dreams as he  says in the stevo podcast pontius grew  up loving the series mutual of omaha's  wild kingdom he and stevo discussed how  they bonded during jackass and wanted to  do a project together so when the stunt  show ended they jeff tremaine and a few  other members of the jackass team  developed the idea of an animal show  done in a way only they could do it as  the hollywood reporter explains wild  boys also helped lead to the making of  jackass number two stevo told the outlet  knoxville joined us for a while  knoxville says have the dog bite me and  shoot me with a nine millimeter gun  while the dog's biting me and tremaine  says to knoxville hey whoa let's not do  this for mtv2 if you have that in you  let's make another movie  another great story pontius describes on  stevo's podcast is how he purposely  called out the wrong group for an award  at the 2003 european vmas pontia says he  kind of got talked into it though he  fully admits that he went through with  the prank because he thought it would be  funny when he opened the envelope to see  the winner was coldplay he first said  the winner was the white stripes as they  got up to receive their award pontius  then said he was kidding and it was  actually coldplay this incident is hard  to find a video of leading one online  commenter to suggest mtv edited it out  of subsequent replays on the podcast  pontius describes how his increased  celebrity and the responsibilities and  privileges that came with it were tough  to handle he describes another awards  show where he and stevo were given  amazing hotel rooms only for pontius to  get extremely drunk and end up passing  out naked on top of an suv outside  returning to the hotel in disgrace  despite all the crazy and many would say  immature stunts that make chris pontius  seem like the living embodiment of peter  pan he has in fact grown up pontius owns  a house has a wife and in 2019 he became  a dad as he announced on instagram on  december 14 2019 i am beyond excited to  announce the birth of my son axe magnus  pontius thank you everybody for your  kind words positivity and inspiration  for all these years shortly after stevo  posted a picture on facebook of himself  his longtime bromantic partner pontius  and acts in a loving embrace stevo wrote  chris is going to be a really great dad  and axe is going to be a very wild boy  given pontius's history of embracing  danger and at times living on a razor  edge the sharp name of axe is pretty  appropriate  in his podcast interview with chris  pontius stevo describes how pontius and  brandon decamillo were the two most  naturally funny guys in the crew joking  about how he always had to do gross and  painful stunts while pontius could carry  less dangerous bits thanks solely to his  sense of humor in fact pontius's sense  of humor and charisma are strong enough  that he's one of the few jackass guys to  also have acted in a few feature roles  he appears as irish henchmen in 2003's  charlie's angels full throttle he plays  black randy the punk legend who started  an la punk label that released songs by  groups including the germs in the darby  crash biopic what we do is secret he  even has a major role in johnny  knoxville's 2018 film action point this  is especially poignant because again  it's proof that the jackass guys really  liked pontius enough to single him out  for inclusion in their personal projects  pontius has several other roles and  while he may forever be known primarily  as a wild boy and a jackass the skater  who became a writer who became a star  who became a dad has shown that  reinvention is just another weapon in  his arsenal  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  jackass are coming soon subscribe to our  youtube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one  you
 

